export anchor ServerRoomStyle:
    number: 412
    screen: DatabaseConsole
    name: Server room
    idea: The console is two equipment racks, with tables as patch panel ports, the open table cabled to its columns, the query on a console LCD, results as LED meters, history as an event log and connections as lit power sockets.
    base: dark
    palette:
        room: #0a0b0d, the page
        frame: #24272c, the rack frames and the sheet border
        rail: #2f3339, mounting rails with dark screw holes
        face: #1a1d22, unit faces and the style sheet
        lcd: #0b1418, displays, log lines and fields
        lcdInk: #bfe9ff, display text
        silk: #e6e8eb, silkscreen labels and text
        muted: #a5abb5, model text, U numbers and units
        green: #4ee08a, OK LEDs, lit meter segments, lit sockets and Run
        onGreen: #04220f, text on green
        amber: #ffc04d, the read-only LED, SQL keywords and focus
        red: #ff7a72, the Fault LED and its error
        blue: #5aa9ff, the patched tasks port, its cable and foreign key columns
        yellow: #f5d547, the key column cable
        grey: #8d949e, plain column cables
    type:
        Industrial condensed sans, DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Barlow Semi
        Condensed, Roboto Condensed, Arial Narrow. Base 14px. Unit titles
        12px bold caps at 0.16em, the app name 22px bold caps. LCDs, log and
        values use ui-monospace, with meter values 22px bold.
    layout:
        A dark aisle header reads BRIGHTWORK DATA and Aisle 3, cabinet for
        production-replica. Two racks sit side by side, each a frame with
        rails on both sides marked with U numbers. Rack A holds a patch
        panel unit with five jacks labelled by table, tasks lit blue with a
        cable dropping into a blue bus, then six column strips in three
        columns, each with a coloured cable stripe and type. Under it a
        console unit with a blinking Ready LED shows the SQL on a dark LCD
        with amber keywords, and raised Run and Clear hardware buttons.
        Rack B holds a Result meters unit with an OK LED and three channels,
        each with the project name, a four segment LED meter lit by count
        and the value, then Rows 3, Time 38 ms and Unit open overdue. Next
        an Event log unit with three LCD lines, a round OK LED or square
        Fault LED, time, name and duration or error. Last a power unit with
        sixteen sockets, fourteen lit, and LEDs for Read-only replica with
        an amber triangle, Lag 2 s and 14 active connections. Below 980px
        the racks stack. On phones rails slim down and the ports wrap.
    spacing: Rack units. 6px between units, 24px rails, 12px by 16px unit padding.
    density: High. Two racks of compact units with many small parts.
    corners: Small. 6px racks, 3 to 4px jacks, buttons and displays, round LEDs.
    borders: A light top and dark bottom edge on each unit face, 2px jack rims, 4px coloured cable stripes.
    shadows: A heavy drop under the racks, a 3px hard ledge under buttons, LED glow and an inset shade in each LCD.
    icons:
        LED shapes carry meaning. Round for OK, square for Fault, triangle
        for read-only, always with the word. A blinking round LED means
        ready and stops when reduced motion is set.
    focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px with a soft amber halo.
    tone: Silkscreened caps, such as Patch panel, Result meters, Event log, Fault and Run.
